# RTS-website Cursor Rules

## Project Structure
- All application code resides in `src/app/` directory
- Next.js App Router uses `src/app/` natively (no top-level app/ shims needed)
- Alias imports use `@/*` pointing to the src directory

## Documentation Rules
- **All markdown documentation files (except root `README.md`) must be placed in `/Documents` directory**
- Keep README.md in the project root
- Organize documentation by topic in `/Documents`
- Use descriptive filenames (e.g., `FEATURE_NAME_IMPLEMENTATION.md`)

## Code Organization
- Server Components by default (no "use client" directive)
- Client Components must have `"use client"` directive and use `.client.tsx` suffix
- Shared utilities in `src/utils/`
- Supabase helpers in `src/utils/supabase/client.ts` and `src/utils/supabase/server.ts`

## Styling
- Centralize styles in `src/app/globals.css`
- Use CSS variables for theming (light/dark mode support)
- Avoid inline styles
- Component-specific styles use `.css` files co-located with components

## Database & Security
- Enable RLS (Row Level Security) on all Supabase tables
- Use `public.is_admin(uuid)` helper function for admin checks
- Store only anon key in client code, never service_role
- All SQL scripts in `/supabase` directory
